{:up ["ALTER TABLE recipes ADD COLUMN tags TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT ''"]
 ;; Extra words to find a Recipe by, which its title does not contain. One TEXT
 ;; column holding whatever the owner typed, following tracker's
 ;; `014-add-task-tags` and rhizome's `items.tags` — **not** a tags table and not
 ;; a join table. The house pattern is why no tag ever needs migrating, splitting
 ;; or deduplicating: there is nothing to keep in step with anything.
 ;;
 ;; `NOT NULL DEFAULT ''` rather than a nullable column, and here the default is
 ;; not a claim about anything the way 004's and 005's were. Untagged is the
 ;; honest reading of a Recipe nobody has tagged: the column records what the
 ;; owner curated, so 'he curated nothing here yet' is the true state of every
 ;; existing row, and there is no third category to preserve. Empty rather than
 ;; NULL also keeps the search clause free of a null case — `instr` on a NULL is
 ;; NULL, which is not `> 0`, so it would work either way, but only one of the two
 ;; is a thing a reader has to check.
 ;;
 ;; **Deliberately not on `recipe_history`.** Tags are not versioned, for the
 ;; reason `published` is not: versions are about content, and a tag is a
 ;; retrieval aid rather than part of the Recipe. Versioning them would put filing
 ;; bookkeeping into the history a reader steps through, and — now that 005
 ;; records provenance — would make a tag tweak count as a whole `ui` version on
 ;; the card's split. So `update-recipe` writes a tag change without archiving
 ;; anything and without moving the version. See the "History model" docstring in
 ;; `et.cb.db.recipe`.
 ;;
 ;; The column is on the row and read by everyone's search but sent to nobody but
 ;; the owner — that half is a projection choice in `select-columns`, not a schema
 ;; one, and it could not be a schema one: the same column has to be searchable
 ;; by an anonymous caller and invisible to them.
 :down ["ALTER TABLE recipes DROP COLUMN tags"]}
